# clang-tidy configuration for the Cupid C sources.
#
# Only checks whose findings are worth a human look on this codebase are
# enabled.  The broad bugprone/modernize/cert groups were evaluated and
# produce thousands of findings that are idiomatic here (unchecked fflush,
# recursion in an interpreter, assignment in conditions) or that would tie
# the sources to C23 (nullptr).  Their auto-fixes also break the build:
# macro-parentheses wraps the bytecode dispatch `goto` in parentheses, and
# use-internal-linkage cannot see cross-file uses through headers.
#
# performance-no-int-to-ptr was also evaluated and dropped.  Every site it
# flags is intrinsic to the interpreter rather than an oversight: the
# `(char *)(-1)` sentinel for an unknown C stack limit in machine.c, the
# StablePtr-to-Pointer conversions the FFI exists to perform in builtin.c
# and iomonad.c, and a hand-rolled offsetof in builtin.c.  None can be
# written without the cast, so the check only ever produced noise.
#
# Run with:  ninja -C build clang-tidy
Checks: >
  -*,
  bugprone-suspicious-realloc-usage,
  bugprone-implicit-widening-of-multiplication-result,
  bugprone-narrowing-conversions,
  bugprone-switch-missing-default-case
WarningsAsErrors: ''
HeaderFilterRegex: '.*'
FormatStyle: none
